@startuml flash-map
' Where an image may live in the 1 MB of flash, and why the linker stops it
' at 510 KB. Grounded in STM32L476RGTX_FLASH.ld (MEMORY), Inc/flash.h
' (FLASH_BANK_BYTES, FLASH_PAGE_BYTES) and industrial-hmi uart-flash-v1.md,
' section 9 (answers 3 and 4).

title Flash map: one image per bank, and the page it must not touch

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #555555

rectangle "Bank mapped at 0x08000000 (the one running)" as running {
  rectangle "image, linked for 0x08000000\n0x08000000 .. 0x0807F7FF\n510 KB = 522240 bytes\n(the linker's FLASH region)" as img1 #E8F0FE
  rectangle "last 2 KB page\n0x0807F800 .. 0x0807FFFF\nCONFIRMED record (piece 6)" as rec1 #FFF4E5
}

rectangle "The other bank, seen at 0x08080000" as other {
  rectangle "the update is written here\n0x08080000 .. 0x080FF7FF\n(piece 5)" as img2 #E8F0FE
  rectangle "last 2 KB page\n0x080FF800 .. 0x080FFFFF\nits CONFIRMED record" as rec2 #FFF4E5
}

img1 -[hidden]down- rec1
img2 -[hidden]down- rec2
running -[hidden]right- other

note bottom of other
  BFB2 (piece 7) swaps which bank sits at 0x08000000,
  so BOTH images are linked for the same address.
  An image larger than 510 KB would reach the record
  page, so it must not link at all: CI links
  tests/oversize_image.c and expects
  "region FLASH overflowed".
end note

@enduml
